msgstr "別の方向を向くときの、柔らかいカサッという音。"

msgid "Edge of the trail"
msgstr "小道の端"

msgid ""
"Edge of the trail: a rustle and a soft thud. Brambles, a hedge or water "
"stop the step."
msgstr "小道の端：カサッという音と柔らかいドスン。イバラ、生け垣、水で先へ進めません。"

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a rustle and a soft thud. Brambles, a hedge or water stop the step."
msgstr "カサッという音と柔らかいドスン。イバラ、生け垣、水で先へ進めません。"

msgid "Befriended"
msgstr "仲良くなった"

msgid ""
"Befriended: a warm rising chime. Your answer matched, and the bird is your "
"friend."
msgstr "仲良くなった：温かく上がっていくチャイム。答えが合って、鳥が友だちになりました。"

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid ""
"a warm rising chime. Your answer matched, and the bird is your friend."
msgstr "温かく上がっていくチャイム。答えが合って、鳥が友だちになりました。"

msgid "New song"
msgstr "新しい歌"

msgid ""
"New song: a soft page turn and a bell. Something new went into your field "
"guide."
msgstr "新しい歌：ページをめくる柔らかい音と鈴。野鳥図鑑に新しいものが載りました。"

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid ""
"a soft page turn and a bell. Something new went into your field guide."
msgstr "ページをめくる柔らかい音と鈴。野鳥図鑑に新しいものが載りました。"

msgid "Not quite"
msgstr "おしい"

msgid ""
"Not quite: two soft, low notes. Your answer did not match, and the bird "
"sings again."
msgstr "おしい：柔らかく低い二音。答えが合わず、鳥がもう一度歌います。"

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
